<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Western India States Agency</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1924">1924</a>–<a href="/years/1947">1947</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> States Agency was a political agency of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-india">British India</a>, formed in 1924 to oversee the many <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathiawar">Kathiawar</a>, Cutch and parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> through a single agent to the Governor-General at Rajkot. Its states, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manavadar">Manavadar</a> and Radhanpur, joined India in 1947–1948.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/western-india-states-agency.jpg" alt="Western India States Agency" width="320" height="262" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joaquin de Salas · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Baroda-gujarat.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
